# Production against an identity provider you have, and the base of production
# with the bundled Keycloak: Handout as the edge, with one certificate per name
# obtained by Caddy itself and an identity provider that is somebody else's. Nothing here obtains a wildcard certificate:
# `*.{$HANDOUT_DOMAIN}` below is a hostname pattern that decides which requests
# a site block answers, and every name it matches gets a certificate of its own.
#
# Two site blocks on purpose. The named one gets an ordinary certificate at
# start; only the pattern block uses on-demand TLS, so the ask endpoint is only
# ever asked about names that could be a handout address. Putting the publisher
# origin or the identity provider through the on-demand path would deny them a
# certificate outright: the ask endpoint answers on the first label, and
# neither "handout" nor "id" is an address.

{$HANDOUT_DOMAIN} {
	import handout-app
}

*.{$HANDOUT_DOMAIN} {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	import handout-app
}
